        "text": "<thinking> To implement the dead_letter.py file that sends failed messages to a dead-letter destination, I will use the AWS SNS (Simple Notification Service) as the concrete external provider. AWS SNS is a fully managed messaging service for both system-to-system and app-to-person (A2P) communications. I will import the boto3 library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, to interact with AWS SNS. The provider will be identifiable by the import of boto3 and the use of AWS SNS-specific functions and parameters. </thinking>\n",
